    "detailed_description": "This is a simple and sometimes tricky 3D puzzle game in which the egg-shaped chicken &quot;Tamaniwatori'' hatches eggs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThere are no time limits or factor that change in real time, so you can play at your own pace.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\u25c7How to play<br />\r\nThe operation is simple, just move the &quot;Tamaniwatori&quot; one square at a time up, down, left, and right.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you step on the egg once and move it one space next to it, a &quot;Tamahiyoko&quot; will be born.<br />\r\nThe level is cleared when all eggs in the field are hatched and the goal is reached.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nVarious mechanisms appear in the levels, such as scaffolding that sinks once you step on it, and scaffolding that appears with a switch.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBe careful if you fall into the water, it will be a mistake and you will have to restart the level from the beginning.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThere may also be an egg-shaped crocodile called &quot;Tamawani&quot; in the level, which is the natural enemy of &quot;Tamawaniwatori&quot;.<br />\r\n&quot;Tamawani&quot; moves along a predetermined route at the same time as &quot;Tamawaniwatori&quot; advances one space. If you get eaten, you will make a mistake, so be careful not to get hit.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs you progress through the game, new worlds will be unlocked and unique mechanisms will increase.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI hope you enjoy it until the end.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n*This game was made in Japan, but most of it can be played regardless of language.",
    "about_the_game": "This is a simple and sometimes tricky 3D puzzle game in which the egg-shaped chicken &quot;Tamaniwatori'' hatches eggs.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThere are no time limits or factor that change in real time, so you can play at your own pace.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\u25c7How to play<br />\r\nThe operation is simple, just move the &quot;Tamaniwatori&quot; one square at a time up, down, left, and right.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nIf you step on the egg once and move it one space next to it, a &quot;Tamahiyoko&quot; will be born.<br />\r\nThe level is cleared when all eggs in the field are hatched and the goal is reached.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nVarious mechanisms appear in the levels, such as scaffolding that sinks once you step on it, and scaffolding that appears with a switch.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nBe careful if you fall into the water, it will be a mistake and you will have to restart the level from the beginning.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nThere may also be an egg-shaped crocodile called &quot;Tamawani&quot; in the level, which is the natural enemy of &quot;Tamawaniwatori&quot;.<br />\r\n&quot;Tamawani&quot; moves along a predetermined route at the same time as &quot;Tamawaniwatori&quot; advances one space. If you get eaten, you will make a mistake, so be careful not to get hit.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nAs you progress through the game, new worlds will be unlocked and unique mechanisms will increase.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nI hope you enjoy it until the end.<br />\r\n<br />\r\n*This game was made in Japan, but most of it can be played regardless of language.",
    "short_description": "This is a simple and sometimes tricky 3D puzzle game in which the egg-shaped chicken &quot;Tamaniwatori'' hatches eggs. While avoiding the natural enemy &quot;Tamawani&quot;, advance on the various scaffolds set up, hatch all the eggs, and aim for the goal.",
